cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  HR from ECG: quality-aware, uncertainty-calibrated heart rate
  and HRV estimation from single-lead ECG
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Soheil
    family-names: Kooklan
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5035-7833'
    affiliation: 'Science and Research Branch, Islamic Azad University (SRBIAU), Tehran, Iran'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/soheilkooklan/HR-from-ECG'
abstract: >-
  HR from ECG estimates heart rate and heart-rate variability from noisy
  single-lead ECG and reports every quantity as an interval rather than a point
  value. It combines a utility-based signal quality index, defined by how much a
  segment degrades the downstream heart-rate estimate rather than by how the
  waveform looks, with a convolutional network whose bottleneck is a
  bidirectional selective state-space model and whose training objective
  includes a differentiable pseudo-periodicity prior. Heart-rate intervals carry
  a distribution-free coverage guarantee through Mondrian conformal prediction
  conditioned on predicted quality, and beat-level uncertainty is propagated to
  HRV indices by conformalised Monte-Carlo ensembles. The system abstains on
  segments that cannot support an estimate.
keywords:
  - electrocardiography
  - heart rate variability
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - signal quality
  - state space models
  - biomedical signal processing
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: 2.0.0
